    <string name="help_select_title">Selecting several tracks</string>
    <string name="help_select_body">On the Tracks tab, the checklist button at the top (or a long press on a track) turns on selection. Tap tracks to select them, then use Play or the ⋮ menu to handle them together: play next, add to the queue or a playlist, add to favorites, share or delete. Back or ✕ ends the selection. The Play and Shuffle icons next to the search box play all tracks in the current order or shuffled; what they do while music is already playing can be set in Settings → Playback.</string>
    <string name="help_import_title">Importing playlists</string>
    <string name="help_import_body">On the Playlists tab, the import button reads .m3u, .m3u8 and .pls playlist files: choose files, or a whole folder (with its subfolders). Each file becomes a playlist with the tracks found in the library, and a summary shows how many were found. The export button saves the playlists you select as .m3u8 files into a folder you choose. Albums, artists and folders can also be saved as a new playlist from their menus.</string>

